eight expert ratings put the race in the safest Democratic tier, and markets price Lamont at 96 to 97 percent, leaving little evidence of a competitive race.", "watch": "A standout debate performance from Fazio or a sharp late shift in the national environment toward Republicans could narrow the gap, though he would need to close a very large deficit in the final weeks.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Ned Lamont (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Connecticut's governor's race pits incumbent Democrat Ned Lamont against Republican Ryan Fazio. Lamont enters the final weeks in a commanding position: every independent poll since June has shown him ahead, and the five surveys conducted in October put his lead between 13 and 23 points among registered and likely voters. Averaged together, the polls put him up roughly 16 points, and betting markets give him about a 96 to 97 percent chance of winning another term.\n\nThe fundamentals reinforce the polling. Connecticut leans Democratic by about eight points, Lamont holds the usual advantages of incumbency, and recent coverage points to voter dissatisfaction with the economy and the Trump administration as a drag on Fazio's campaign. Ratings outlets unanimously place the race in the safest Democratic category. The first debate in late October is the main remaining opportunity for Fazio to alter the race's trajectory.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.994, "margin": 15.28}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9913, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9896, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9893, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9879, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9857, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9868, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9861, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9879, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_